ah, delivered and connected on-site. The exact specs are below — fuel consumption, output, footprint — so you can confirm this is the right size before you book.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Call now: <a href=\"tel:+971 56 921 3754\">+971 56 921 3754</a></strong></p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">What a 100 kVA Generator Powers</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">A 100 kVA set gives you around 80 kW of continuous usable load. Realistic uses:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Mid-size construction site</strong> — site offices, hoists, welding sets, power tools and floodlighting running together</li>\n<li><strong>Small commercial building on backup</strong> — lighting, lifts, essential HVAC and IT for a few floors during an outage</li>\n<li><strong>Medium event or exhibition</strong> — stage lighting, AV, catering equipment and cooling for a mid-size setup</li>\n<li><strong>Retail or showroom standby</strong> — keeps a store fully operational through a grid cut</li>\n<li><strong>Workshop or small factory</strong> — several machines, compressors and lighting on one supply</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If your total load is above roughly 70 kW, step up to a 150 kVA set — or for large industrial jobs, a <a href=\"/products/500kva-generator-hire/\">500 kVA generator</a> or other heavy duty generator is the better fit. If you&#8217;re well under 50 kW, a smaller portable unit will cut your fuel and generator rental cost — talk to our team.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">100 kVA Generator Specifications</h2>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Specification</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime output</td>\n<td>100 kVA / 80 kW</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Standby output</td>\n<td>110 kVA</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Voltage</td>\n<td>400V 3-phase / 230V single-phase</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Full-load current</td>\n<td>144 amps at 400V, 3-phase</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Frequency</td>\n<td>50 Hz</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speed</td>\n<td>1500 rpm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Power factor</td>\n<td>0.8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Engine options</td>\n<td>Cummins, Perkins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Enclosure</td>\n<td>Silent canopy or open-frame</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Noise level</td>\n<td>~76 dB(A) at 7 metres (silent canopy)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">100 kVA Generator Fuel Consumption</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Fuel is usually the biggest cost on a rental, so plan around it. Approximate diesel use for a 100 kVA set by load:</p>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Load</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Power drawn</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Fuel use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>20 kW</td>\n<td>~7 litres/hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>40 kW</td>\n<td>~12 litres/hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75%</td>\n<td>60 kW</td>\n<td>~17 litres/hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>80 kW</td>\n<td>~22 litres/hour</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Most sites run near 50% load, so expect roughly 12 litres/hour — around 288 litres on a 24-hour day. Standard units carry a 200-litre base tank; larger external tanks are available for longer runtime. We quote fuel as a separate line item, so there are no billing surprises.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Dimensions, Weight &amp; Site Placement</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Know the footprint before delivery day so the unit fits and can be placed safely:</p>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Specification</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Silent (canopied)</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Open-frame</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Length</td>\n<td>2.4 m</td>\n<td>1.9 m</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Width</td>\n<td>0.86 m</td>\n<td>0.74 m</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Height</td>\n<td>1.57 m</td>\n<td>1.56 m</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Weight</td>\n<td>~1,600 kg</td>\n<td>~1,150 kg</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Placement requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Firm, level ground able to take ~1.6 tonnes</li>\n<li>Delivered by hiab/crane truck — needs clear access for offloading</li>\n<li>Clearance around the unit for airflow and exhaust dispersal</li>\n<li>Silent canopy runs at ~76 dB at 7 m — suitable for events, hotels and occupied buildings</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">What&#8217;s Included With Every 100 kVA Rental</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Every unit arrives ready to run:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Diesel tank</li>\n<li>Distribution board</li>\n<li>Manual or automatic changeover switch</li>\n<li>Cables and cable ramps</li>\n<li>Delivery, installation and on-site testing</li>\n<li>24/7 support for the rental period</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Cable and breaker sizing is handled by our technicians on-site — a 100 kVA set typically pairs with a 160A–200A main breaker, sized to your actual load and cable run.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Contact us for a quote: +971 56 921 3754</strong></p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Silent vs. Open-Frame 100 kVA</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Silent / acoustic</strong> — our fully enclosed <a href=\"/products/silent-generator/\">silent generator</a> runs at ~76 dB at 7 m, for events, hospitals, hotels and residential-adjacent sites</li>\n<li><strong>Open-frame</strong> — lower cost, faster to deploy, best for open construction sites and industrial yards</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Both available for immediate hire across the UAE.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">FAQs</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How many amps is a 100 kVA generator?</strong> 144 amps at 400V, 3-phase, 50 Hz. On single-phase 230V the figure differs — tell us your connection and we&#8217;ll confirm.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How much fuel does a 100 kVA generator use per hour?</strong> Around 12 litres/hour at 50% load and up to ~22 litres/hour at full load, depending on your load profile.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What can a 100 kVA generator run?</strong> About 80 kW of load — a mid-size construction site, a small building on backup, or a medium event. Above ~70 kW, size up to 150 kVA.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How big is a 100 kVA generator?</strong> A silent 100 kVA unit is roughly 2.4 m long, 0.86 m wide and 1.57 m high, weighing about 1,600 kg. It needs firm level ground and crane/hiab access for placement.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What&#8217;s the minimum rental period for a 100 kVA generator?</strong> We offer short-term and long-term rentals — get in touch with your project dates and we&#8217;ll confirm terms.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Rent a 100 kVA Generator Today</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Need 80 kW of reliable power on-site fast? We deliver 100 kVA generators across Dubai, Abu Dhabi and Sharjah with same-day dispatch on standard sizes — part of our full <a href=\"/services/generator/rental-generator-in-uae/\">rental generator in UAE</a> fleet.</p>\n<p><a href=\"tel: +971 56 921 3754\"><strong>+971 56 921 3754</strong></a></p>\n','http://localhost:8000/storage/media/1-1.jpg','default','published','100 kVA Generator Rental UAE | 80 kW Diesel Genset Hire','Rent a 100 kVA diesel generator in UAE - 144 amps, ~22 L/hr fuel use, delivered across Dubai, Abu Dhabi & Sharjah. Cummins & Perkins units.',NULL,'https://rentalpower.ae/products/100-kva-generator-rental/','100 kVA Generator Rental UAE | 80 kW Diesel Genset Hire','Rent a 100 kVA diesel generator in UAE - 144 amps, ~22 L/hr fuel use, delivered across Dubai, Abu Dhabi & Sharjah. Cummins & Perkins units.','http://localhost:8000/storage/media/1-1.jpg',1,'100 kva generator rental in uae',91,100,'2026-10-17 04:49:54','2026-10-18 02:18:09',NULL),(145,1,'100 kVA Generator Rental in UAE','100-kva-generator-rental','<p dir=\"ltr\">A 100 kVA <a href=\"/products/diesel-generator/\">diesel generator</a> delivers 80 kW of usable power — enough to run a mid-size construction site, a small commercial building on backup, or a medium event. <a href=\"/\">Rental Power</a> supplies serviced, load-tested 100 kVA units from Cummins and Perkins across Dubai, Abu Dhabi and Sharjah, delivered and connecte