ong> — separate units per temperature band, so frozen and chilled stock stay properly separated</li>\n<li><strong>Cold rooms</strong> — modular walk-in rooms, where a container doesn&#8217;t fit the space available</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Wide temperature band from deep freeze to controlled ambient in one unit</li>\n<li>Delivered, positioned and running the same day</li>\n<li>Insulated on all sides for stable temperature in UAE heat</li>\n<li>Digital set-point control with temperature display</li>\n<li>Options including ramps, strip curtains and internal lighting</li>\n<li>Remote temperature monitoring available</li>\n<li>Low-humidity storage that protects stock from condensation and mould</li>\n<li>Delivery within 24–48 hours, no minimum hire period, and 24/7 breakdown support</li>\n<li>Serviced and temperature-tested before every hire</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Applications</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Cold room breakdown cover</strong> — keeping stock safe while permanent refrigeration is repaired</li>\n<li><strong>Seasonal and peak capacity</strong> — extra storage for Ramadan, event seasons or peak trading</li>\n<li><strong>Food service and retail</strong> — restaurants, hotels, catering operations and supermarkets</li>\n<li><strong>Pharmaceutical and medical storage</strong> — temperature-controlled holding for sensitive goods</li>\n<li><strong>Events and hospitality</strong> — on-site chilled and frozen storage for catering operations</li>\n<li><strong>Construction and remote sites</strong> — cold storage where no permanent facility exists</li>\n<li><strong>Logistics and distribution</strong> — buffer storage during transit or warehouse work</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Rental Availability in UAE</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Rental Power supplies refrigeration units and cold storage for short-term and long-term hire across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the wider UAE, delivered ready to plug in and run. Where a project needs chilled water for building or process cooling rather than cold storage, our <a href=\"/services/cooling/rental-chiller-in-uae/\">chiller rental in UAE</a> range covers that side, and units can be supplied with a <a href=\"/services/generator/rental-generator-in-uae/\">rental generator</a> where site power isn&#8217;t available.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Choosing the Right Option</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Work out pallet positions, not floor area</strong> — cold storage is planned by how much stock you need to hold.</li>\n<li><strong>Separate your temperature bands</strong> — frozen and chilled stock in one unit means compromising on both. Two units is usually the right answer.</li>\n<li><strong>Check your power supply</strong> — these units need three-phase power and run continuously. Check capacity before delivery day.</li>\n<li><strong>Check access and ground</strong> — a 40ft unit needs truck access and firm, level ground to sit on.</li>\n<li><strong>Plan for door traffic</strong> — frequently opened doors lose temperature; strip curtains help significantly.</li>\n<li><strong>Ask about monitoring</strong> — for pharmaceutical or high-value stock, remote temperature monitoring and alarms are worth specifying.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">FAQs</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What temperature range can these units hold?</strong> Standard refrigerated containers typically run from about -25°C to +25°C, covering frozen, chilled and controlled-ambient storage.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What power supply do they need?</strong> Three-phase power, typically in the 380–460V range. We&#8217;ll confirm the exact requirement for the unit you hire, and can supply a generator if site power isn&#8217;t available.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How much can a unit hold?</strong> Roughly 11 pallets in a 20ft unit and 23 in a 40ft unit, depending on stack height and configuration.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How quickly can one be delivered?</strong> Typically within 24 to 48 hours of the hire being agreed. Once on site, a unit is running and pulling down to temperature within hours of being connected.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Can I hire one for just a few days?</strong> Yes. There&#8217;s no fixed minimum hire period, so we&#8217;ll quote for the days you actually need — whether that&#8217;s a weekend event or a year of extra storage.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What if it fails with my stock inside?</strong> Call us, day or night. Breakdown support runs 24/7 for the length of the hire, which is the whole point of hiring cold storage from a rental company rather than buying a unit outright. Call the moment a temperature reading looks wrong rather than waiting to see if it settles — the earlier we know, the more of your stock we can save.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">CTA</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Need cold storage in the UAE?</strong> Tell us the temperature you need, how much stock you&#8217;re holding and for how long, and we&#8217;ll get the right unit to your site within 24 to 48 hours, backed by 24/7 support. <strong>Call <a href=\"tel: +971 56 921 3754\">+971 56 921 3754</a></strong> or request a quote.</p>\n','/storage/media/tempraray-ac-in-uae.jpg','default','published','Refrigeration Unit Rental in UAE - Rental Power and Rental Cooling in UAE','Rent portable air Refrigeration unit rental UAE and stay cool this season. We offer efficient systems for any setting.+971 56 921 3754',NULL,'https://rentalpower.ae/products/refrigeration-unit-rental-uae/','Refrigeration Unit Rental in UAE - Rental Power and Rental Cooling in UAE','Rent portable air Refrigeration unit rental UAE and stay cool this season. We offer efficient systems for any setting.+971 56 921 3754','/storage/media/tempraray-ac-in-uae.jpg',1,'refrigeration unit rental in uae',91,100,'2026-10-17 04:49:54','2026-10-18 02:18:09',NULL),(153,1,'Portable Chiller Rental in UAE','products/portable-chiller-rental-uae','<p dir=\"ltr\">A portable chiller is a compact, self-contained cooling unit built to be moved, positioned and started quickly — usually wheeled or skid-mounted, with an integral pump and tank so it needs nothing but power and a hose connection. Where a large chiller is a plant installation, a portable unit is equipment you place where the heat is. It&#8217;s the right tool for spot cooling, single-process duties, small venues and jobs that move around a site.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">What Makes This Equipment Different?</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Size and self-sufficiency, not just mobility.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">A portable chiller carries its own pump and fluid reservoir on board, so there&#8217;s no separate pump set to size or install. It rolls or lifts into position, connects to a standard site supply on smaller units, and runs. Larger fixed chillers need positioning by crane, external pumps, manifolds and a commissioning crew.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The trade-off is capacity. Portable units cover the lower end of the range — small spot coolers sit around 1–5 TR, and portable process chillers commonly run up to around 30–40 TR. Above that you&#8217;re into skid-mounted <a href=\"/products/air-cooled-chiller-rental-uae/\">air-cooled chillers</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">They also handle glycol duty well, which matters for process work. Many portable units are specified to run a water-glycol mix for leaving temperatures below 0°C, which a standard comfort-cooling chiller won&#8217;t do.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Key Specifications</h2>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Specification</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Capacity range</td>\n<td>Around 1 TR to 30–40 TR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Leaving fluid temperature</td>\n<td>Below 0°C on glycol-capable units</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fluid</td>\n<td>Water or water-glycol mix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compressor type</td>\n<td>Scroll</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Refrigerant</td>\n<td>Varies by unit; confirmed at enquiry</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Power supply</td>\n<td>Smaller units single-phase; larger units 400V / 3-phase</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pump and tank</td>\n<td>Integral pump and reservoir on board</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mobility</td>\n<td>Locking castors on smaller units; skid or trailer mount on larger</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Condenser</td>\n<td>Air-cooled; no tower or water supply needed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Control</td>\n<td>Digital thermostat with set-point control</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><em>Exact specifications vary by unit and are confirmed at the time of enquiry based on your load and site conditions.</em></p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Available Capacities / Options</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Spot coolers (around 1–5 TR)</strong> — server rooms, control rooms, single workstations, small retail units</li>\n<li><strong>Small process chillers (around 5–15 TR)</strong> — laser cutters, injection moulding, laboratory and medical equipment, food production lines</li>\n<li><strong>Mid portable chillers (around 20–40 TR)</strong> — small venues, temporary offices, multi-machine process loads</li>\n<li><strong>Glycol-spec units</strong> — for below-zero leaving temperatures on process duty</li>\n<li><strong>Multiple units</strong> — several portables spread across a site instead of one central machine, so each area is controlled independently</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Moves on locking castors or lifts on a skid — no crane for smaller units</li>\n<li>Integral pump and reservoir, so nothing extra to size or install</li>\n<li>Runs on site power; smaller units on a standard supply</li>\n<li>Air-cooled — no cooling tower, no water connection</li>\n<li>Glycol-capable units available for below-zero process duty</li>\n<li>Set-point control with stable temperature holding</li>\n<li>Redeployable — move it to the next area when the job changes</li>\n<li>Delivery within 24–48 hours, no minimum hire period, and 24/7 breakdown support</li>\n<li>Serviced and tested before every hire</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Applications</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Process cooling</strong> — holding machinery, moulds or production fluid at temperature</li>\n<li><strong>Server and control rooms</strong> — emergency cooling when building HVAC fails</li>\n<li><strong>Food and beverage production</strong> — temperature-critical stages on smaller lines</li>\n<li><strong>Laboratories and medical equipment</strong> — steady cooling for heat-generating instruments</li>\n<li><strong>Small events and temporary offices</strong> — chilled water for a single AHU or fan coil</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance cover</strong> — keeping one area cool while permanent plant is serviced</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Rental Availability in UAE</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Rental Power supplies portable and mobile chillers for short-term and long-term hire across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the wider UAE, delivered ready to connect. For loads beyond what a portable unit carries, this equipment sits within our wider <a href=\"/services/cooling/rental-chiller-in-uae/\">chiller rental in UAE</a> range, so we can move you up to a larger skid-mounted machine whenever the job needs it.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Choosing the Right Option</h2>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Work out the heat load, not the room size</strong> — process cooling is sized on the heat your equipment produces.</li>\n<li><strong>Check the fluid temperature you need</strong> — below 0°C means a glycol-spec unit.</li>\n<li><strong>Check the power you have</strong> — small units may run single-phase, but larger ones need three-phase.</li>\n<li><strong>Think about where the heat goes</strong> — an air-cooled portable rejects heat into the space around it, so indoor use needs ducting or ventilation.</li>\n<li><strong>Consider several small units instead of one large one</strong> — independent control per area, and no single point of failure.</li>\n<li><strong>If the load is above roughly 40 TR</strong> — an <a href=\"/products/air-cooled-chiller-rental-uae/\">air-cooled chiller</a> is the better fit.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">FAQs</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What&#8217;s the difference between a portable chiller and a spot cooler?</strong> A spot cooler blows cold air directly into a space. A portable chiller cools a fluid loop that then feeds equipment or an air handler. Different jobs.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Can it run below zero?</strong> With a glycol mix and a unit specified for it, yes. Confirm the leaving temperature you need when enquiring.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Does it need a water supply?</strong> No. The loop is closed and the condenser is air-cooled. You fill the reservoir at start-up and top up as needed.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Can I use it indoors?</strong> Yes, but the heat it removes has to go somewhere. Indoor placement usually needs ducted condenser discharge or adequate ventilation.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>How mobile is it really?</strong> Smaller units roll on locking castors and move by hand. Larger portables are skid-mounted and need a forklift or tail-lift.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"></h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Need a portable chiller in the UAE?</strong> Tell us the heat load, fluid temperature and power available on site, and we&#8217;ll match the right unit — delivered within 24 to 48 hours, for as long or short a period as you need. <strong>Call <a href=\"tel:+971 56 921 3754\">+971 56 921 3754</a></strong> or request a quote.</p>\n','/storage/media/pot.jpg','default','published','Portable Chiller Rental in UAE - Rental Power and Rental Cooling in UAE','Stay comfortable at your event with our high-performance Portable chiller rental cooling solutions. No installation required.+971 56 921 3754',NULL,'https://rentalpower.ae/products/portable-chiller-rental-uae/','Portable Chiller Rental in UAE - Rental Power and Rental Cooling in UAE','Stay comfortable at your event with our high-performance Portabl